use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../../behaviors/FormParticipation import FormParticipation
from ../../../behaviors/Presence import Presence
from ../../collections/List import List
from ../../overlays/Popover import Popover

export ui-component Select:
    description:
        A select lets the user pick one value from a fixed list of options. The
        list stays hidden until the user opens it, and picking an option sets
        the value and closes the list.

    composes:
        - @{Popover}
        - @{List}

    behaviors:
        - @{FormParticipation}
        - @{Presence}

    closed:
        When closed, it shows the current value, or a placeholder such as
        "Choose a country" if there isn't one. The placeholder is not a label;
        the select still has its own name.

    opening:
        The user opens it by clicking it, or from the keyboard. Which keys
        open it is up to the chosen library. When it opens, the current value
        is highlighted and scrolled into view, or the first option if there is
        no value. The list is at least as wide as the select.

    choosing:
        Moving through the open list with the arrow keys only highlights
        options; it doesn't change the value. Clicking an option, or pressing
        Enter on the highlighted one, sets the value and closes the list.
        Escape closes it without changing anything. Either way, focus goes
        back to the select.

    typeAhead:
        Typing letters, whether the list is open or closed, jumps to the first
        option starting with what was typed. Nothing is hidden.

    options:
        Options can be put in groups under headings. Headings can't be picked.
        Disabled options are shown but can't be picked.

    clearing:
        The component decides whether the value can be cleared back to
        nothing. A select that must have a value can't be cleared.

    readOnly:
        A read-only select shows its value and can be focused, but can't be
        opened to change it. A disabled one can't be focused or opened.

    autofill:
        The component can say what kind of value it holds, such as a country,
        so the platform can fill it in along with the rest of an address. How
        this is done is up to the chosen library.

    nonGoals:
        - No typing to search and narrow the list. That's a Combobox
        - Not for picking several values
